mcp__flow - nexus__agent_spawn({ type: 'coder', name: 'Response Generator' });

// 3. Create linear workflow
mcp__flow -
  nexus__workflow_create({
    name: 'Ticket Processing',
    steps: [
      { id: 'classify', action: 'classify', agent: 'researcher' },
      { id: 'resolve', action: 'resolve', agent: 'coder' },
      { id: 'escalate', action: 'escalate', agent: 'coder' },
    ],
    triggers: ['manual'],
  });

// 4. Execute (synchronous)
mcp__flow -
  nexus__workflow_execute({
    workflow_id: 'workflow_id',
    input_data: { ticket: 'sample' },
  });
```

**Limitations in this pattern:**

- Only two agent types available
- No parallel processing – tickets are processed one at a time
- No dependency management – steps always run in the order defined
- No real-time confidence check step – all tickets either respond or escalate via manual rule

